<Project>

    <!--
        Solution-wide build defaults.

        XML documentation is generated for every project so that:
          - the API reference (Scalar/OpenAPI) can surface controller and DTO summaries, and
          - the compiler flags documentation that references parameters which no longer exist (CS1572).

        Noise from the convention-driven docs is suppressed:
          - CS1591: missing XML comment for a publicly visible member (we don't document everything).
          - CS1573: a parameter has no matching param tag (params are documented only when not self-evident).
    -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591;CS1573</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!--
        Analyzer and nullable ratchet.

        Nullable is on for every project. A project that is not annotated yet sets
        <Nullable>disable</Nullable> in its csproj and is listed in build/nullable-allowlist.txt.
        scripts/check-nullable-allowlist.sh fails when the two disagree, so the list can only shrink.
    -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <AnalysisLevel>latest-recommended</AnalysisLevel>
        <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!--
        The DroneDB (libddb) build Registry is built and tested against.

        This is the only place it is written. scripts/ddb-release.sh reads it for everything that
        installs libddb, downloads exactly this build and checks it with sha256sum -c:
          - CI installs the .deb (scripts/ddb-release.sh fetch-deb);
          - the Dockerfile installs the same .deb (fetch-deb, token as a build secret for a CI build);
          - Registry.Web.csproj embeds the Windows zip in Windows builds (release: downloaded by
            MSBuild; ci: fetch-windows-zip) and fails the build when its SHA256 differs.
        scripts/ddb-release.sh check (CI) fails when the pin is malformed or written elsewhere, or
        when anything downloads releases/latest. Startup checks the ABI of the loaded library
        (DdbAbi: libddb 2.x, ABI major 2, minor >= 10), not this version number.

        DdbSource:
          release  a published release: DdbVersion, and the SHA256 of ddb_<DdbVersion>_amd64.deb and
                   ddb-<DdbVersion>-Windows.zip (the "digest" of each asset, or SHA256SUMS, in
                   gh api repos/DroneDB/DroneDB/releases/tags/v<version>). Remove the Ci and
                   ArtifactId properties.
          ci       an unreleased DroneDB CI build (c-cpp.yml): the DroneDB commit, its run, the ids
                   of its "Linux-Binaries" and "Windows Binaries" artifacts
                   (gh api repos/DroneDB/DroneDB/actions/runs/<run>/artifacts), DdbVersion as that
                   build names its files, and the SHA256 of the .deb and of the zip inside them.
                   Downloading an artifact needs DRONEDB_ARTIFACT_TOKEN (see scripts/ddb-release.sh);
                   artifacts expire 90 days after their run.

                   DdbDebFileVersion (optional, ci only): the version in the .deb file name when it is
                   not DdbVersion. DroneDB names the .deb of an untagged build <package.json
                   version>~git<commit> (scripts/build-debian-package.sh; the commit is the pull
                   request merge commit for a PR run), e.g. ddb_2.0.0~git1813815_amd64.deb next to
                   ddb-2.0.0-Windows.zip. Remove the property with the move to the release.

        Pinned now (2026-11-25): the DroneDB v2.13.0 release (ABI 2.13; the handshake requires ABI 2.13:
        DdbAbi.Minor 13). 2.13.0 keeps no artefact cache: a user GeoTIFF is read in place once the raster helper has
        decoded it whole in its sandbox, any other raster through a copy that lives as long as its reader, and the
        tiles of a photo are drawn from the photo for each request; artefactCacheMb is accepted and has no effect.
        It adds DDBCleanupCache, the removal of the tiles, downloads, DSM tiles and leftover folders older than their
        ages, which the nightly cache cleanup job runs.
        2.12.0 counts the statistics of the uploaded file of a GeoRaster in its COG build
        (the sourceStatistics member of the raster.cog artifact, which DDBBuildRasterStatistics also writes for an
        older build) and gives the value info of an entry with them (DDBGetRasterValueInfoEx2), so the first value
        info of a built raster reads no pixel.
        2.11.0 lists the formulas of a raster with its raster info, without its statistics;
        computes the exact statistics of a raster in one parallel pass of ddb-tilers 0.14.0 (ddbtRasterStatistics);
        says whether the COG of a built GeoRaster has its statistics next to it (the statistics member of the
        raster.cog artifact) and writes them on request (DDBBuildRasterStatistics), which the nightly completeness
        check uses for the COGs built before libddb wrote them at build time.
        2.10.0 adds DDBFindCoverage, the images whose footprint sees a GeoJSON point, line
        or polygon, ranked by how close the middle of the image is to it, with the approximate pixel of the
        place in each image, which the coverage endpoint (the Photos tab of an annotation) uses; a point cloud
        in a local CRS says that its CRS is local (ddb-tilers 0.13.5 refuses its tiles with the same words).
        2.9.0 adds DDBRescanEx2, the rescan of a list of entry paths (a file, or a folder
        for the entries under it), each entry re-read outside the writer lock of the index and committed on
        its own, which the rescan of selected entries (rescan-entries) uses; the adapter calls it for every
        rescan. 2.8.1 draws a point-cloud map tile
        zoomed in past the density of the cloud as a surface (ddb-tilers 0.13.4) and builds the 3D Tiles of
        an OBJ whose statements are indented with a tab, as ODM writes them (Obj2Tiles v1.10.4). 2.8.0
        builds the COPC of a geographic or geocentric point cloud in a projected CRS (the crs of its build artifact), ignores
        a CRS the coordinates do not fit, and rebuilds once the COPCs and COGs that change (the
        completeness sweep queues them); its gdal-util speaks protocol 1.4. 2.7.2 writes palette and
        masked rasters as 2.6.0 did (their colour table, mask and overviews); 2.7.1 gives the exported and region
        GeoTIFFs the metadata, scale and offset of their source again, which 2.7.0 lost. 2.7 reads the
        rasters of the process with ddb-tilers, runs the operations on users' rasters (mask, merge,
        alignment, the photos of the splat export) in the raster helper on the user's file, and no
        longer links PDAL. 2.6 added the DDBConfigure setting artefactCacheMb (Ddb:ArtefactCacheMb), the
        bound of libddb's artefact cache, which an older libddb refuses. The SHA256 values are those of
        the release's SHA256SUMS.
    -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <DdbSource>release</DdbSource>
        <DdbVersion>2.13.0</DdbVersion>
        <DdbDebSha256>0a797f9f8c6619b172e99366ce48fa9299301bab7a2adf5ce029a5a7899d79d5</DdbDebSha256>
        <DdbWindowsZipSha256>61f887529db78995e5fd649396b28b36999d2f7236231d19b8cf2cf06614c083</DdbWindowsZipSha256>
    </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
